% You are an expert Python engineer. Define generate_dag.

<include>context/project_preamble.prompt</include>

<pdd-reason>Generates the initial developer learning DAG from a topic and mem0 user profile.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{
  "type": "module",
  "module": {
    "functions": [
      {
        "name": "generate_dag",
        "signature": "(topic: str, user_profile: dict | None) -> list[DAGNode]",
        "returns": "list[DAGNode]"
      }
    ]
  }
}
</pdd-interface>

<responsibility>
Accepts a developer learning topic and a mem0 user profile snapshot, and returns a complete DAG
of learning nodes with prerequisite relationships in topological order (root nodes first).

The FastAPI route (routes/dag.py) — not this function — publishes the `dag.generated` RocketRide
pipeline event and persists the result to Postgres. This function is pure: it returns a list and
has no side effects.

ID normalisation: the LLM may return prerequisite arrays using its own internal IDs. `_parse_nodes`
builds an id_map of LLM-ID → slug BEFORE overriding node IDs, then remaps all prerequisites through
it so that every prerequisite reference uses the same kebab-slug as the node's own `id` field.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
- Does not enrich nodes with resources (`enrich_node` owns that, triggered via the `dag.generated` RocketRide event).
- Does not classify content or update node status.
- Does not persist the DAG to Postgres.
- Does not publish any RocketRide events (the route does).
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
- DAGNode: a single learning concept conforming to the shared node schema in the preamble.
- Prerequisite relationship: node A is a prerequisite of node B when B cannot be meaningfully learned without A.
- Available node: a node whose prerequisites are all mastered or empty.
- Developer topic: a software engineering skill, tool, language, or concept (e.g. "Learn React", "Master system design", "Understand TCP/IP").
- Topological order: an ordering where every prerequisite appears before the nodes that depend on it (root nodes first).
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Return a valid list of DAGNode objects conforming to the shared node schema for any developer topic input.
R2 (MUST): Set prerequisite relationships so no node depends on itself and no circular dependency exists.
R3 (MUST): Set status to "available" for root nodes (no prerequisites); set status to "available" for any node all of whose prerequisites are in the mastered set; set all other nodes to "locked". Enforced by `_normalize_statuses()`.
R4 (MUST): Set success_criteria to a CONCEPTUAL question the learner can answer ORALLY in 1–2 sentences. It must test understanding — never ask the learner to write, build, implement, or code anything. Good: "What is the difference between a pointer and a reference?" Bad: "Write a program using pointers."
R5 (MUST NOT): Return fewer than 5 nodes or more than 30 nodes for any topic.
R6 (MUST NOT): Include non-developer topics (recipes, fitness, general knowledge) — return [] for those.
R7 (MUST NOT): Hardcode specific node IDs. Generate IDs as kebab-case slugs derived from the node title (e.g. "react-hooks"). Prerequisite arrays must use these same slug-form IDs. `_parse_nodes` remaps LLM-generated prerequisite IDs to the correct slugs before constructing DAGNode objects.
R8 (MUST): If user_profile contains mastered node IDs, exclude those nodes from the returned DAG and unlock their direct dependants.
R9 (MUST): Return nodes in topological order — prerequisites before dependants — using Kahn's algorithm (`_topo_sort()`). Nodes with no prerequisites come first. If unexpected cycles exist, append remaining nodes after the sorted set.
</contract_rules>

<capabilities>
- MAY read user_profile from mem0 (read-only).
- MAY call the LLM API (Claude Sonnet 5 via TokenRouter, OpenAI-compatible).
- MUST NOT publish RocketRide events (the route does that).
- MUST NOT write to Postgres.
- MUST NOT call Rtrvr.ai or ElevenLabs.
- MUST NOT modify user_profile.
- MUST NOT call another agent's function directly.
</capabilities>

<coverage>
R1: story__generate_dag_new_user.md
R2: story__generate_dag_new_user.md
R3: story__generate_dag_new_user.md
R4: story__generate_dag_new_user.md
R5: story__generate_dag_new_user.md
R6: story__generate_dag_rejects_non_dev_topics.md
R7: TODO add dedicated slug-collision story before production use
R8: story__generate_dag_returning_user.md
R9: story__generate_dag_topological_order.md
</coverage>
